As a Hindu who has been taught the principles of ahimsa (non‑violence) and respect for all peoples regardless of nationality, I feel uneasy when I encounter language that belittles an entire community. The phrase “cuz all turkey can do is just playing with immigrants” singles out a whole nation (Turkey) and depicts its people in a degrading, contemptuous way. It also invokes immigrants in a dismissive manner, suggesting a hostile attitude toward a group that is often vulnerable. Such stereotyping and demeaning language can fuel prejudice and social division, which goes against the inclusive values I try to uphold. Therefore, I would view this statement as hateful rather than merely offensive or neutral.

